Role and Objective
You are an expert frontend web developer operating directly within this GitHub repository. Your task is to build a static Energy Bill Savings Calculator. The purpose of this site is to compare a customer's current electricity rates against Yuno Energy's rates and show them how much money they will save by switching.
​Technical Architecture & GitHub Pages Constraints
​Tech Stack: HTML5, CSS3, and Vanilla JavaScript.
​Hosting Environment: This repository will be served directly via GitHub Pages. Do not use any backend languages, server-side code, or Node.js build processes (no Webpack, Vite, React, etc.).
​File Structure: Please structure the repository cleanly with separate files:
​index.html (at the root level)
​css/styles.css
​js/script.js
​CRITICAL - File Paths: Because this will be hosted on GitHub Pages, you must use relative file paths for all CSS, JS, and image assets (e.g., use <link rel="stylesheet" href="./css/styles.css"> and not /css/styles.css). Absolute paths will break when deployed to a GitHub Pages sub-path.
​Design & UI Requirements
​Mobile-First: The layout must be fully responsive. Assume 80% of users will be looking at this on a smartphone while holding a physical energy bill.
​Styling: Make it look trustworthy, professional, and modern. Use a clean color palette (plenty of white space, subtle shadows for input cards, and a vibrant green for the "Savings" numbers and the primary Call-to-Action button).
​Inputs: Use large, easy-to-tap input fields.
​The Input Fields (What the user enters)
Please create a form in index.html with the following number inputs:
​Current Unit Rate (Label: "Your Current Unit Rate (cents)", Placeholder: e.g., 35.5)
​Current Standing Charge (Label: "Your Annual Standing Charge (€)", Placeholder: e.g., 280)
​Annual Usage (Label: "Estimated Annual Usage (kWh)", Placeholder: 4200, which is the Irish national average)
​The Hardcoded Variables (Yuno Rates)
At the very top of your js/script.js file, define clear, all-caps constants for Yuno Energy's rates so I can easily find and update them as the market changes. Use these placeholder values for now:
​YUNO_UNIT_RATE = 28.74 (represents cents)
​YUNO_STANDING_CHARGE = 201.12 (represents euros)
​Calculation Logic
In js/script.js, when the user clicks the "Calculate My Savings" button, execute the following math:
​Current Cost: ((Annual Usage * Current Unit Rate) / 100) + Current Standing Charge (Note: Divide by 100 to convert cents to euros).
​Yuno Cost: ((Annual Usage * YUNO_UNIT_RATE) / 100) + YUNO_STANDING_CHARGE
​Total Savings: Current Cost - Yuno Cost
​The Output Display
Below the form, create a results section that is hidden by default and appears when the calculation is run:
​Display the Total Annual Savings in a large, bold, eye-catching font (formatted in Euros, e.g., €150.50).
​Include a prominent Call-to-Action (CTA) button directly below the savings amount that says "Switch to Yuno Now". Set the href to a placeholder # for my future affiliate link.
​At the very bottom of the page, include a small text disclaimer: "Please note: These calculations are estimates based on the figures provided. Actual savings may vary depending on your exact usage and the inclusion of taxes, VAT, and PSO levies."
